<%#
  A panel end-cap: the bar the app draws with Panel's ::before / ::after.

  locals: side - "top" or "bottom", which inward edge gets the radius.

  Email has no pseudo-elements, so the cap is a real row inside the frame. Two
  differences from the app, both forced:

  - It sits flush against the inside of the border rather than straddling it at
    top:-2px. Nothing in a table can overlap a border.
  - The inset is a flat 12% rather than max(10px, 12%). max() is unsupported,
    and the floor only mattered below ~83px wide.

  An mj-divider, not a styled cell: MJML gives a divider an explicit width and
  centre, which is exactly a cap inset equally from both sides.
%>
<mj-section padding="0" background-color="transparent">
  <mj-column padding="0">
    <mj-divider border-width="<%= MailerTheme::CAP_HEIGHT %>"
                border-style="solid"
                border-color="<%= MailerTheme::ENDCAP %>"
                width="<%= MailerTheme::CAP_WIDTH %>"
                align="center"
                padding="0"
                css-class="cap-<%= side %>" />
  </mj-column>
</mj-section>
